/ Inside plang's own goals an "each goal" event doesn't run while event.setting.goal is app (the default): Read reads
/ %!goal% three times, each read running plang's shortcut goal (/system/shortcut/goal.goal), and "before each goal" runs
/ Count for Loop and each Read, never for the shortcut goal. With event.setting.goal all, it runs for each shortcut goal
/ too. Count keeps its count in .data/count.txt beside the test: a shortcut's variables end with its call, a file
/ doesn't, and .data/ holds what a run leaves.
Start
- set %items% = [1, 2, 3]
- save 0 to file ".data/count.txt"
- before each goal, call Count
- call Loop
- read file ".data/count.txt", write to %count%
- assert %count% equals 4, "under app: Loop and the three Reads, none of plang's own goals"
- set %!app.event.setting.goal% = "all"
- save 0 to file ".data/count.txt"
- call Loop
- read file ".data/count.txt", write to %count%
- assert %count% equals 7, "under all: the three shortcut goals too"
- delete file ".data/count.txt"

/ Reads %!goal% once for each item.
Loop
- foreach %items%, call Read

/ One read of %!goal%, a shortcut plang answers with a goal of its own.
Read
- set %seen% = %!goal%

/ The event's call: one more in .data/count.txt.
Count
- read file ".data/count.txt", write to %count%
- set %count% = %count% + 1
- save %count% to file ".data/count.txt"
